            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today (Monday, **August 3, 2026**), the most notable “Azure AI”–related items showing up in news and official update feeds are:\n\n## Biggest news item today (customer / Azure + AI)\n- **ArcelorMittal expanded its partnership with Microsoft**, naming **Azure as its primary cloud platform** as it accelerates a company-wide push around data + AI capabilities and broader digital transformation. ([thenextweb.com](https://thenextweb.com/news/arcelormittal-microsoft-azure-primary-cloud-ai))\n\n## Recent (past week) Microsoft/Azure AI-related headlines\n- **Microsoft earnings / Azure AI demand**: Reporting around Microsoft’s most recent earnings call highlights **strong AI-driven Azure demand** and continued infrastructure expansion to support AI workloads. ([finance.yahoo.com](https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/msft-q4-earnings-call-highlights-140000543.html))  \n- **Model ecosystem on Foundry**: Coverage notes **Moonshot AI’s Kimi K3** reaching enterprise users via **Fireworks on Microsoft Foundry**, giving Azure customers a managed path to run the model. ([technode.com](https://technode.com/2026/07/30/moonshot-ais-kimi-k3-reaches-enterprise-users-through-fireworks-on-microsoft-foundry/))  \n- **AI security**: Several outlets have covered Microsoft’s **AI security initiatives** (including “Project Perception” coverage) in the last week. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/money/technologyinvesting/microsoft-escalates-the-ai-security-race-with-project-perception-and-a-new-in-house-model/ar-AA28OuAb))  \n- **AI infrastructure for inference**: Reporting also mentions Microsoft plans involving **AMD “Helios”** for AI inference on Azure. ([msn.com](https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/technology/microsoft-to-roll-out-amd-helios-for-ai-inference-on-azure/ar-AA28odHr))  \n\n## Official “what changed today” pointers (best for Azure AI service changes)\n- **Azure Updates (official feed)** is the most reliable place to see *today’s* product/service updates across Azure (including AI-adjacent services). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- The **Azure AI tag on the Azure Blog** shows the latest official AI posts/announcements (not necessarily posted today, but it’s the canonical stream). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/tag/ai/))  \n- A third-party consolidated feed also lists new Azure updates posted today (useful for scanning, then confirm in the official Azure Updates entry). ([azurecharts.com](https://azurecharts.com/updates?monthback=0))  \n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure AI Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI**, **Azure AI Search**, **Copilot** on Azure, or *anything Azure+AI*), I can narrow this to just the relevant “today” items.",
